opulation so there was little to tie  them together  that was until Napoleon came back he was  reinstated as the French Emperor marched  his army into the Netherlands where he  met a new coalition at the Battle of  Waterloo Napoleon lost now this new  kingdom had a unifying foundation  story.this couldn't wash away the  religious differences though and so  William invited the southern Nobles to  vote on a notion of religious equality  throughout the kingdom  unfortunately for William they voted no  William however devised an ingenious  plan to get around this he ignored their  complaint and counted all of their votes  as yeses William was a much gentler  ruler than Napoleon had been but that's  not to say he tolerated much dissent and  he was quick to censor the press when it  criticized him over the next decade  Williams policies didn't really please  anyone  he chose Dutch as the kingdom's official  language which annoyed the French  speakers in the south he wanted both  religions to be equal yet subservient to  the state which annoyed everyone he was  his economic policies that  really upset those living in the south  though taxes were raised to pay for the  kingdom's debt and around half of the  country's tax revenue came from the  south yet only about 30% of government  spending went to it which felt like  money was simply being funneled to the  north it actually wasn't not really it  was simply being funneled to the king in  his inner circle hundreds of thousands  of people in the south petitioned the  king to address their issues in the late  1820s but they got nothing from him  tensions in the south continued to rise  until the 25th of August 1830 in which  rioting broke out in Brussels this came  just after the Bourbon dynasty in France  was ousted by similar riots in Paris  the Wrights in Brussels soon turned to  revolution and the royal government in  its troops were soon forced north the  southern Netherlands then declared  itself to be an independent nation  taking the name Belgium taken from the  regions name in Latin the great powers  of Europe eyeing the situation with  great interest in the end though no  great power got involved since Britain  decided to host the London conference in  late 1830 to decide what would be done  neither the Dutch nor the Belgians were  invited in case you were wondering the  French proposed that they would annex  this territory Prussia would gain  Luxembourg in all of this and the rest  of the South would be formed into a  British protectorate this was firmly  rejected by Britain because France  wasn't allowed to have nice things  instead the great powers recognized the  independence of Belgium which would also  include this territory taken from  Luxembourg Belgium would also get itself  a fancy new King Leopold the first  chosen because he had no ties to either  France or Prussia William the first and  the Dutch didn't accept this agreement  and instead decided to invade the south  and take the provinces back by force his  army defeated the new and poorly  organized Belgian army but was forced to  turn back after only ten days when the  French sent their forces north to stop  him the Dutch held on to Maastricht in  Antwerp the latter of which was besieged  and captured by the French in 1832 this  meant that when William finally accepted  Belgian independence in 1839 he was  granted the territory of Limburg and was  made its Duke  so the United Kingdom of the Netherlands  was no more now there were two kingdoms  which had to find their way in Europe  after basically bankrupting itself the  Netherlands had to institute  constitutional reforms which William  couldn't accept and so he abdicated in  favor of his son will in the second as  for Belgium it's important to note that  the people who lived there did see  themselves as Belgians and there wasn't  much support for either reunification  with the north or for joining France  Belgium was largely seen though by the  great powers as little more than a  buffer state between France and Prussia  which is why it was declared to be  permanently neutral furthermore to  protect this neutrality Britain formally  gara  it's Independence a guarantee that  Britain would honor 75 years later I  hope you enjoyed this episode and thank  you for watching a special thanks to  James Bissonnette Ozark a flash Henry  Robin Winston Cawood Adam Harvey and  Skye Chappell  you
 

